<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Mountain Republic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mountainous Republic of the Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> was a state formed by the mountain peoples of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechens">Chechens</a>, Ingush, Dagestanis and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Circassians</a>, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution">Russian Revolution</a>. It declared independence in May 1918 and sought Ottoman support. Denikin's White army overran it in 1919, and the Bolsheviks took the region in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus.jpg" alt="Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus" width="320" height="188" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arsenekoumyk · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Mountain_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
